"1. Build one yearly comparison\nFor each financial year, calculate:\n- Marketing spend: sum of amount.\n- Revenue: sum of gross_amount − discount_amount − refund_amount, using\ncompleted orders only.\n- Purchasing customers: distinct customers with completed orders.\nSummarise each file by year separately, then combine the summaries. This avoids\nrepeating marketing expenditure against every order.","fontSize":20,"baseFontSize":null,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"1. Build one yearly comparison\nFor each financial year, calculate:\n- Marketing spend: sum of amount.\n- Revenue: sum of gross_amount − discount_amount − refund_amount, using completed orders only.\n- Purchasing customers: distinct customers with completed orders.\nSummarise each file by year separately, then combine the summaries. This avoids repeating marketing expenditure against every order."

